 "notes": "Cenote Angelita is an open, round pit about 25–30 m across (cave-ha.com, Mexico Desconocido) and 56–60 m deep, with fresh water to about 30 m, a hydrogen sulphide cloud about 3 m thick at 27–30 m and salt water below, where the chamber widens under the vertical walls (first-hand observation). A mound of collapse debris with dead trees rises from the bottom to about 27 m near the middle and pokes through the cloud. OpenStreetMap has no outline, so the shoreline is a 27 m circle; the entry is by stairs to the water, placed on the north rim only because the access track arrives from the north, and every position is approximate.",
